  "challenge": "Several of the cited policies point to a remediation or approval path rather than hard rejection: PO-001’s own rationale is that totals over threshold “require manager approval,” not automatic denial; IN-002 states the dead SKU is “payable only after explicit reactivation,” which is a human workflow, not a terminal reject; and VN-001 flags an unknown vendor as a fraud entry point but does not by itself forbid onboarding a first-time supplier. get_prior_invoice and get_vendor_invoice_history show no prior adverse outcome on INV-1003 or Fraudster LLC—only an absence of history—while FR-001/FR-002 are LOW/MEDIUM tells that the corpus treats as signals to scrutinize, not sole grounds to kill the invoice. Read together, the packet is built for human vendor-verification and approval routing (ESCALATE), and REJECT over-closes paths the policies leave open.",
  "proposed_outcome": "ESCALATE",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["PO-001", "IN-002", "VN-001", "FR-001", "FR-002"]
}
